    "access": {
      "value": "You are a kobold with the kobold or kobold heritage, a dragon instinct barbarian, or a draconic bloodline sorcerer."
    },
    "special": {
      "value": "You can't select another dedication feat until you have gained two other feats from the dragon disciple archetype. If you later take the sorcerer archetype, you must choose the draconic bloodline.\nLeads to: Breath of the Dragon|APG, Claws of the Dragon|APG, Disciple's Breath|APG, Draconic Scent|APG, Dragon Arcana|APG, Scales of the Dragon|APG, Shape of the Dragon|APG, Mighty Dragon Shape|APG, Wings of the Dragon|APG, Cloud Walk|SoT3, Deflecting Cloud|SoT3, Mighty Wings|SoT3, Shape of the Cloud Dragon|SoT3"
    },
    "descriptions": {
      "value": [
        {
          "resource_id": "levelled_description",
          "stats": {
            "id": "levelled_description_0f3d7569d656",
            "level": {
              "value": 2
            },
            "description": {
              "value": "You choose to study or worship one type of dragon, and your focus grants you a measure of its power. You become trained in arcane spell DCs and arcane spell attack rolls. Choose one color of dragon when you select this feat; if you are a sorcerer with the draconic bloodline, this must be the same type as your bloodline. You gain resistance equal to half your level against one type of damage determined by the chosen dragon type. The GM may allow you to choose a dragon type not listed below, and will determine the damage type appropriate for that dragon.\n\n- **Black, Brine1, or Copper** Acid\n- **Blue, Bronze, Cloud1, or Sky1** Electricity\n- **Brass, Gold, Magma1, Red, or Underworld1** Fire\n- **Crystal1 or Forest1** Piercing\n- **Green** Poison\n- **Sea1** Bludgeoning\n- **Silver or White** Cold\n- **Sovereign1** Mental\n- **Umbral1** Negative\n\n1Mwangi Expanse, p.76\n\nYou also gain a +1 circumstance bonus to saving throws against sleep effects and effects that would make you paralyzed."
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
